# intra-dcsize-luma-var0-runtime.meta
source_path: video/msmpeg4/reference/binaries/wmpcdcs8-2001/mpg4c32.dll
source_sha256: aedb4cf3d33c8554ab8acf04afe2d936eaa7c49107c5fefe163bca2e94b3c099
tool: ud-emulator (univdreams 539f04e4be5ed90519885da7267d483ad6c0dbaf) round27_msmpeg4_watch harness + provenance/sandbox-03/tools/codebook.py
method: the codec was run in the sandbox (MP43 decode of provenance/sandbox-02/encode-gradient-pq8.bin);
  after the frame the guest heap (0x60000000..0x600c0000) was read back post-mortem and the
  decoder's own runtime VLC decode tables (descriptor +0x14 root table, +0x18 (width, table)
  pair array; walked exactly as the VLC reader 0x1c219351..0x1c2193b9 walks them) were
  expanded into (code, bit_length) -> symbol. This is the effective codebook the decoder
  uses; it equals the packed .data source read as: u32 count, then count x (u32 code LE,
  u32 bit_length LE) starting at source+4 (verified record-for-record, 0 mismatches).
  NOTE: the earlier region_05f0d8_dcsize.csv/.meta of the same table read the records as
  (bit_length, code) starting at +8, which pairs each record's length with the NEXT
  record's code; its bit_length column is correct, its code column is not.
kind: intra_dc_differential_vlc_runtime
columns: symbol, code_bin, bit_length
semantics: symbol == DC differential magnitude (0x1c216d22: movzx al); symbol 119 is the
  ESC index (8-bit raw magnitude follows, 0x1c216d67); a sign bit follows every non-zero
  magnitude (0x1c216d34). Bound when [this+0x8bc] == 0 (luma, header dc-size selector 0).
